    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The fix is complete! I've resolved the floating-point precision issue in three places:\n\n1. **`src/money.js` - `parseEuros()`**: Changed from `Number(...).toFixed(2) * 100` to `Math.round(Number(...) * 100)`\n2. **`src/money.js` - `cellCents()`**: Changed from `Number(s) * 100` to `Math.round(Number(s) * 100)`  \n3. **`src/locale.js` - `decimalCommaToCents()`**: Changed from `parseFloat(...) * 100` to `Math.round(parseFloat(...) * 100)`\n\nThe root cause was that JavaScript's floating-point arithmetic caused 39.95 \u00d7 100 to produce 3995.0000000000005 instead of exactly 3995. Using `Math.round()` ensures the result is always a whole number of cents.\n\nI've tested it with your Gym (39.95), Netflix (12.99), and Spotify (10.99) examples\u2014all now store correctly as whole cents.\n\nWould you like me to commit this fix?",
